ede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and March to April came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 139% of normal in June to July and 32% in September to October. Grid 11535 had its driest year in 2011 at 45% of normal. A preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 12134 reads 9.3, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
